# Workspace Structure & File Placement

## Decision Flow

```
New file or folder needed
  ├─ AI development (AI app, MCP, AI tool)? → ai/
  ├─ ACM/QE work (test cases, automation, clusters, JIRA)? → automation/
  ├─ Cross-cutting reference (both AI and QE)? → notes/
  └─ Temp download or unknown? → downloads/ (sort later)
```

## Root Summaries

| Root | Purpose | Key Paths |
|------|---------|-----------|
| `automation/` | ACM QE: test automation, cluster ops, documentation | `documentation/`, `qe-automation-repos/`, `dev-team-repos/`, `tools/` |
| `ai/` | AI apps, MCP servers, AI tooling | `ai_systems/` (monorepo), `tools/mcp/` |
| `notes/` | Cross-cutting notes, knowledge DB mirror | `notes.md`, `reference/`, `knowledge/` (read-only mirror) |
| `downloads/` | Temp landing zone (ephemeral) | Never reference as canonical |

## Mandatory Placement Rules

```
RULE 1: NEVER create files at workspace root level
RULE 2: Secrets → automation/tools/automation-workspace/secrets/<type>/
RULE 3: Investigation reports → <root>/documentation/investigations/<topic>-<date>/
RULE 3b: Screenshots/snaps → automation/documentation/investigations/snaps/
         Name: <jira-key>-<description>.png
RULE 4: Git clones: QE → qe-automation-repos/, Dev → dev-team-repos/, AI → ai/
RULE 5: New MCP servers → ai/tools/mcp/<name>/ (MUST update README.md)
RULE 6: Temp files → automation/tools/automation-workspace/tmp/
RULE 7: Cluster configs → automation/tools/automation-workspace/configs/<cluster>/
RULE 8: Test cases → automation/documentation/acm-components/<area>/test-cases/<version>/
RULE 9: If unsure → ASK the user
```

## Naming Conventions

- Investigation dirs: `<topic>-<monYYYY>` (e.g., `bm11b-sep2025`)
- Test case dirs: by ACM version (`2.16/`, `2.17/`)
- Git clone dirs: match upstream repo name
- No loose files at root -- everything in a subdirectory

## automation/ Structure

```
automation/
  .cursor/rules/          # Context-triggered rules (.mdc)
  documentation/          # ALL written docs
    guides/               # Human index, Google Doc mirrors
    processes/            # Workflow docs, DOCUMENTATION-INDEX.md
    acm-components/       # Per-component docs + test-cases/
    architecture/         # Architecture docs, rhacm-docs clone
    investigations/       # Time-boxed reports + snaps/
    archive/              # Cold storage
  qe-automation-repos/    # QE test repos (clc-ui, console-e2e, etc.)
  dev-team-repos/         # Upstream repos (console, etc.)
  tools/                  # Scripts, installers, configs (see tools/README.md)
```

## ai/ Structure

```
ai/
  ai_systems/          # stolostron/acm-ai-qe monorepo clone
  tools/mcp/              # MCP server installations (Cursor uses these)
  additional-apps/        # Standalone AI side projects
  documentation/          # AI workspace docs
```

## Documentation Maintenance

If a task changes directory layout or documented paths: update the nearest `README.md`, root `README.md` when placement rules change, and any `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` that encode those paths. Full checklist: `workspace-documentation-maintenance.mdc`.
